Drop the ``CuraProfile`` wrapper and the OrcaSlicer-to-CuraEngine key translation map (ADR-008). ``[slicer.cura.overrides]`` now passes through to CuraEngine verbatim — rename orca-style keys to their CuraEngine equivalents: ``wall_loops`` → ``wall_line_count``, ``top_shell_layers`` → ``top_layers``, ``bottom_shell_layers`` → ``bottom_layers``, ``sparse_infill_density`` → ``infill_sparse_density``, ``nozzle_temperature`` → ``material_print_temperature``, ``bed_temperature`` → ``material_bed_temperature``, ``initial_layer_print_height`` → ``layer_height_0``. The hardcoded ``adhesion_type = "none"`` baseline is also removed so setting ``adhesion_type = "brim"`` in TOML now reaches CuraEngine (#586).
